  "challenge": "ESCALATE is unnecessary: PR-001 already fires on a clear, mechanical overcharge (WidgetB $541.50 vs $500 ref, 8.3% > 5% tolerance) whose policy rationale is simply 'Overcharge relative to contracted price,' and this invoice is even listed as the corpus example for that code. The packet has no PO, quote, note, or prior-invoice pattern that could justify a higher agreed price—get_vendor_invoice_history returns zero prior invoices and get_prior_invoice finds no earlier submission of INV-1014—so there is nothing for a clerk to confirm. With an active vendor but empty price-acceptance history and no on-invoice authorization for the overage, the evidence already supports rejecting and requesting a corrected invoice or credit rather than holding for human review.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["PR-001"]
}
